// C-string entry points stop at NUL. Calendar byte entry points retain explicit
// length for scanning, including the reference's nested strcmp/strchr behavior.
// Buffers are caller-owned C strings: capacity includes NUL; writes truncate.
// Pure kernels use no runtime JS values, allocations, or exceptions. The explicit
// host entry point observes libc environment/files and the native platform clock.
